        <obo:IAO_0000115>A one-carbon compound with formula CO&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt; in which the carbon is attached to each oxygen atom by a double bond. A colourless, odourless gas under normal conditions, it is produced during respiration by all animals, fungi and microorganisms that depend directly or indirectly on living or decaying plants for food.</obo:IAO_0000115>
