        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_50846"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An agent that suppresses immune function by one of several mechanisms of action. Classical cytotoxic immunosuppressants act by inhibiting DNA synthesis. Others may act through activation of T-cells or by inhibiting the activation of helper cells. In addition, an immunosuppressive agent is a role played by a compound which is exhibited by a capability to diminish the extent and/or voracity of an immune response.</obo:IAO_0000115>
